<!--Render Target Documentation — LeafOptimization
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.LeafOptimization-->
<rdoc:LeafOptimization xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Direct mb_block call for single-NativeBlock types
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Some block types are a single NativeBlock: every property maps 1:1 to
    native settings, no sub-blocks, no multi-child composition. Example:
    com.machineblocks.bml.bricks.Standard.

    Standalone compile of such a block emits a direct mb_block() main call.
    Customizer variables are the settings. There is no typed wrapper module and
    no mb_param_* extraction layer:

        mb_block(
            config = mb_config,
            settings = [
                ["size", size],
                ["studs", studs]
            ]
        );

    This avoids the extra module call found in older hand-maintained SCAD
    artifacts. Composite blocks with real inner structure (Wall, Calibrator)
    still emit typed modules.

    Exactly one NativeBlock child uses this direct call. Zero children returns
    files: [] and diagnostic MB_EMPTY_BLOCK. Two or more children use the
    composite module in CompositeRendering. A leaf parameter that is not a
    property reference, or a default other than a boolean, number, string, or
    SizeXYZ, returns files: [] and diagnostic BML_LEAF_VALUE_UNSUPPORTED.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:CompositeRendering" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:LeafOptimization>
